Unix utility 'touch'

The Unix utility 'touch' creates a new, empty file at a given path, absolute or relative
to the current directory, on the mounted disk. Only an administrative (root) user can
run it. The file is not created if it already exists, its path is invalid, or its name
is longer than 12 characters.

USAGE:

touch <path>

No additional parameters are required.

For more information, enter 'touch ?' or 'touch --help'.

HISTORY

This command appeared in the Hexagonix Mineru development branch (2026).

